# .dockerignore — what NOT to send to the Docker build context.
#
# Without this file the context is ~1.4 GB (build/ 896M, recapture-api/ 206M,
# .dart_tool/ 146M, recapture/ 55M, .git/ 17M). With it, the context is ~5 MB
# and `docker build` starts instantly.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER add these — the Flutter web build genuinely needs them:
#
#   pubspec.yaml  pubspec.lock  analysis_options.yaml
#   lib/  web/  assets/
#   .env  .env.dev  .env.staging  .env.prod
#       ^ these four are declared under `flutter: assets:` in pubspec.yaml.
#         Excluding any one of them fails the build with
#         "no file or variants found for asset: .env".
#         The Dockerfile OVERWRITES them with build-arg values before
#         compiling, so nothing from your local machine is baked in.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Version control / editors / CI ───────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
*.iml

# ── Build outputs and tool caches (regenerated inside the image) ─────────────
build/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.packages
coverage/
.last_build_id

# ── Platform folders irrelevant to a web build ──────────────────────────────
android/
ios/
linux/
macos/
windows/

# ── Not part of the app ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
test/
docs/
fastlane/
Gemfile
Gemfile.lock
maya-viewer/
recapture/
recapture-api/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# ── Docker's own files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT nginx.conf — stage 2 does `COPY nginx.conf` and the build fails without
# it ("/nginx.conf: not found"). The Dockerfile and .dockerignore themselves
# are read by the builder outside the context, so excluding them is safe.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml

# ── Root-level notes and scratch files (nextPrompt.txt alone is 600 KB) ─────
# NOTE: these globs do not cross "/", so they match ROOT level only —
#       an asset such as assets/data/foo.txt is still included.
*.md
*.txt
Makefile
